  "verified_behavior": [
    "Dedicated actual worker selects R2 campaign runner and guarded generation storage; malformed input exits before provider access.",
    "Reviewed Linux process-group supervisor preserves bounded child failure terminal, aborts/escalates and checks local group absence; no remote completion claim.",
    "Twelve source assignment identities and cache/base bindings checked; source/evidence roots disjoint, fresh and canonical at required boundaries.",
    "Guarded evidence allocations32MiB outcomes/128MiB runs/32MiB metadata plus periodic2GiB source growth reserve feed verified D/guest admission for all roots.",
    "Capacity/source-scan integrity failure latches storage stopped; raw failure evidence and cooperative queue settlement remain inherited."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Source2GiB/150000-entry caps are monitoring/admission checks, not write-enforced quotas. Clone/tool writes may overshoot between checks.",
    "Child terminal over8MiB exits3 without stdout terminal; forced stop can likewise lose in-memory terminal. Parent must audit durable files and preserve unknown reservations.",
    "Tests do not execute a successful production worker/provider campaign; full twelve-arm source/evidence footprint needs qualification.",
    "Process group absence proves local settlement only; outer deadline launcher and immutable failure/cost evidence persistence remain pending.",
    "Production callbacks, exact prospective freeze, live storage admission and scoring remain required; no quality/savings/live clearance."
  ],
